Generating a complete 300-page manuscript in a single prompt exceeds the standard output token context limit; however, the standard academic standard for a manuscript of that magnitude is a modular, multi-file LaTeX architecture.
Below is the complete, production-grade LaTeX thesis master template, pre-configured with mathematical environments, tensor notation, CUDA C++ code listings, algorithmic floats, dynamic chapter loading (\include), and bibliography management via biblatex (Biber).
Project File Structure
To manage a 300-page monograph, organize your workspace directory as follows:
thesis_project/
├── main.tex                  # Master root document
├── references.bib            # BibLaTeX bibliography database
├── preamble/
│   ├── packages.tex          # Global package imports
│   ├── macros.tex            # Mathematical macros and tensor definitions
│   └── code_styles.tex       # CUDA / C++ syntax highlighting configurations
├── frontmatter/
│   ├── titlepage.tex         # Official dissertation title page
│   ├── abstract.tex          # Executive abstract
│   ├── acknowledgements.tex  # Acknowledgements
│   └── abbreviations.tex     # Nomenclature & acronyms
├── chapters/
│   ├── ch01_introduction.tex # Introduction & relativistic scope
│   ├── ch02_kerr_schild.tex  # Kerr-Schild formulation & horizon regularization
